[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2989737022","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107730#issuecomment-2989737022","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107730","id":2989737022,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yM8Q-","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T04:08:38Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T04:08:38Z","body":">One extremely simple solution that resolves both issues but has an impact on performance is to simply apply nonlinear sRGB encoding before color correction and debanding and convert back to linear encoding before returning from the tonemapping shader\n\nThis seems like a good way. Since LUT relies on srgb for lookup, convert to srgb is necessary.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e45cc68092906465df3ea9e820a7c77d602addb1/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/renderer_scene_render_rd.cpp#L677\n\nMaybe we can get a srgb view of color correction texture if hdr 2d is enabled, which can avoid converting the result back to linear","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2989737022/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991450934","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107730#issuecomment-2991450934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107730","id":2991450934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yTes2","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T12:44:14Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T16:39:09Z","body":"When HDR 2D is enabled, I think that the Debanding function should be applied in the blit shader just after this line: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5abed52fd9d99c4aab7d8c62d505f9ad618e4533/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/blit.glsl#L120\n\nI haven’t tested this, but conceptually this is where this dither function was originally designed to be placed, according to the slides from Valve. This should be a better approach than converting to/from nonlinear sRGB encoding in the tonemap shader. Applying dither in the tonemap shader only makes sense when quantization is happening immediately after.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991450934/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992644727","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107730#issuecomment-2992644727","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107730","id":2992644727,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yYCJ3","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T19:54:59Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T20:23:22Z","body":"I've updated my [proof of concept fix](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/master...allenwp:godot:vulkan-nonlinear-color-correction-dithering) to simply apply dithering in blit just before quantization and it works well, but has performance implications, especially for HDR 2D.\n\n> Maybe we can get a srgb view of color correction texture if hdr 2d is enabled, which can avoid converting the result back to linear\n\nThis is beyond my current understanding of the codebase, so please feel free to look into this approach or any other approach that will be higher performance than what I have in my proof of concept branch.\n\nEdit: Opened a PR: #107782","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992644727/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]